rentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path><path d="M2.75 15.25L7.25 10.75" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path></svg></button>
<span data-as="p">For each one: what the three sources say, and where it lives in dev-skills.</span>
<h3 class="flex whitespace-pre-wrap group font-semibold" id="1-you-set-the-goal-and-the-check-then-step-away"><div class="absolute" tabindex="-1"><a href="#1-you-set-the-goal-and-the-check-then-step-away" class="-ml-10 flex items-center opacity-0 border-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100 focus:outline-0 group/link" aria-label="Navigate to header">​<div class="size-6 rounded-md flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-white/50 dark:bg-background-dark dark:brightness-[1.35] dark:ring-1 dark:hover:brightness-150 bg-white ring-1 ring-gray-400/30 dark:ring-gray-700/25 hover:ring-gray-400/60 dark:hover:ring-white/20 group-focus/link:border-2 group-focus/link:border-primary dark:group-focus/link:border-primary-light"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="size-3 shrink-0"><path d="M8.50001 6.827C8.14801 6.995 7.81801 7.225 7.52701 7.517L7.51701 7.527C6.13601 8.908 6.13601 11.146 7.51701 12.527L9.69201 14.702C11.073 16.083 13.311 16.083 14.692 14.702L14.702 14.692C16.083 13.311 16.083 11.073 14.702 9.692L13.771 8.761" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path><path d="M9.50002 11.173C9.85202 11.005 10.182 10.775 10.473 10.483L10.483 10.473C11.864 9.092 11.864 6.854 10.483 5.473L8.30802 3.298C6.92702 1.917 4.68902 1.917 3.30802 3.298L3.29802 3.308C1.91702 4.689 1.91702 6.927 3.29802 8.308L4.22902 9.239" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path></svg></div></a></div><span class="cursor-pointer">1. You set the goal and the check, then step away</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>OpenAI:</strong> “Humans steer. Agents execute.” (<a href="https://openai.com/index/harness-engineering/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">Harness engineering</a>)</li>
<li><strong>Anthropic:</strong> “Give Claude a check it can run… It’s the difference between a session you watch and one you walk away from.” (<a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/best-practices" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">Claude Code best practices</a>)</li>
<li><strong>Lauren Tan:</strong> “Give the agent a goal and a way to check it, in your own words.” (<a href="https://github.com/cursor/plugins/blob/main/pstack/docs/guide/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">pstack guide</a>)</li>
</ul>
<span data-as="p">Without a check it can run, the agent’s only signal is that the work looks done, and you become the test loop. In dev-skills this is phase B, taken one step further: verify.md is a full set of scenarios, written before any code, reviewed by another model, and frozen.</span>
<h3 class="flex whitespace-pre-wrap group font-semibold" id="2-one-agent-owns-the-work-end-to-end"><div class="absolute" tabindex="-1"><a href="#2-one-agent-owns-the-work-end-to-end" class="-ml-10 flex items-center opacity-0 border-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100 focus:outline-0 group/link" aria-label="Navigate to header">​<div class="size-6 rounded-md flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-white/50 dark:bg-background-dark dark:brightness-[1.35] dark:ring-1 dark:hover:brightness-150 bg-white ring-1 ring-gray-400/30 dark:ring-gray-700/25 hover:ring-gray-400/60 dark:hover:ring-white/20 group-focus/link:border-2 group-focus/link:border-primary dark:group-focus/link:border-primary-light"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="size-3 shrink-0"><path d="M8.50001 6.827C8.14801 6.995 7.81801 7.225 7.52701 7.517L7.51701 7.527C6.13601 8.908 6.13601 11.146 7.51701 12.527L9.69201 14.702C11.073 16.083 13.311 16.083 14.692 14.702L14.702 14.692C16.083 13.311 16.083 11.073 14.702 9.692L13.771 8.761" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path><path d="M9.50002 11.173C9.85202 11.005 10.182 10.775 10.473 10.483L10.483 10.473C11.864 9.092 11.864 6.854 10.483 5.473L8.30802 3.298C6.92702 1.917 4.68902 1.917 3.30802 3.298L3.29802 3.308C1.91702 4.689 1.91702 6.927 3.29802 8.308L4.22902 9.239" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path></svg></div></a></div><span class="cursor-pointer">2. One agent owns the work end to end</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>OpenAI:</strong> in their own repo, given a single prompt, “the agent can now” go from reproducing a bug to merging the fix, and “escalate to a human only when judgment is required.” (<a href="https://openai.com/index/harness-engineering/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">Harness engineering</a>)</li>
<li><strong>Anthropic:</strong> “A well-designed single agent with appropriate tools can accomplish far more than many developers expect.” (<a href="https://claude.com/blog/building-multi-agent-systems-when-and-how-to-use-them" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">Building multi-agent systems</a>)</li>
<li><strong>Lauren Tan:</strong> “Code-coupled work (one feature, one migration) goes to a single owner.” (<a href="https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack/skills/poteto-mode" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">pstack playbooks</a>)</li>
</ul>
<span data-as="p">Every handoff loses context; one stripped nearly 600 lines from my plan. In dev-skills this is <code>deliver</code>: the owner can hand coding, checks or scenario runs to subagents, but it integrates the work and makes the calls. That’s why I set Agent Lord aside. Work still happens in parallel, but one owner coordinates it.</span>
<h3 class="flex whitespace-pre-wrap group font-semibold" id="3-the-agent-can-run-operate-and-observe-the-real-product"><div class="absolute" tabindex="-1"><a href="#3-the-agent-can-run-operate-and-observe-the-real-product" class="-ml-10 flex items-center opacity-0 border-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100 focus:outline-0 group/link" aria-label="Navigate to header">​<div class="size-6 rounded-md flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-white/50 dark:bg-background-dark dark:brightness-[1.35] dark:ring-1 dark:hover:brightness-150 bg-white ring-1 ring-gray-400/30 dark:ring-gray-700/25 hover:ring-gray-400/60 dark:hover:ring-white/20 group-focus/link:border-2 group-focus/link:border-primary dark:group-focus/link:border-primary-light"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="size-3 shrink-0"><path d="M8.50001 6.827C8.14801 6.995 7.81801 7.225 7.52701 7.517L7.51701 7.527C6.13601 8.908 6.13601 11.146 7.51701 12.527L9.69201 14.702C11.073 16.083 13.311 16.083 14.692 14.702L14.702 14.692C16.083 13.311 16.083 11.073 14.702 9.692L13.771 8.761" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path><path d="M9.50002 11.173C9.85202 11.005 10.182 10.775 10.473 10.483L10.483 10.473C11.864 9.092 11.864 6.854 10.483 5.473L8.30802 3.298C6.92702 1.917 4.68902 1.917 3.30802 3.298L3.29802 3.308C1.91702 4.689 1.91702 6.927 3.29802 8.308L4.22902 9.239" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path></svg></div></a></div><span class="cursor-pointer">3. The agent can run, operate and observe the real product</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>OpenAI:</strong> “we made the app bootable per git worktree, so Codex could launch and drive one instance per change.” (<a href="https://openai.com/index/harness-engineering/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">Harness engineering</a>)</li>
<li><strong>Anthropic:</strong> left to itself, their agent passed unit tests without noticing the feature didn’t work end to end. It did much better once told to “do all testing as a human user would.” (<a href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/effective-harnesses-for-long-running-agents" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">Effective harnesses for long-running agents</a>)</li>
<li><strong>Lauren Tan:</strong> a verification skill is “critical infrastructure rather than ‘just’ a skill.” (<a href="https://x.com/poteto/status/2094457600259842065" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">The Complete Guide to pstack, Pt. 1</a>)</li>
</ul>
<span data-as="p">Unit tests check the code you thought to test. Driving the real app also checks the wiring, the defaults and the entry points, which is where my late bugs came from. In dev-skills this is phase A, plus the scenarios in verify.md: each runs from the entry point the user actually uses and records what the old code does, which catches a check that could never fail.</span>
<h3 class="flex whitespace-pre-wrap group font-semibold" id="4-plans-and-progress-live-in-files-in-the-repo"><div class="absolute" tabindex="-1"><a href="#4-plans-and-progress-live-in-files-in-the-repo" class="-ml-10 flex items-center opacity-0 border-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100 focus:outline-0 group/link" aria-label="Navigate to header">​<div class="size-6 rounded-md flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-white/50 dark:bg-background-dark dark:brightness-[1.35] dark:ring-1 dark:hover:brightness-150 bg-white ring-1 ring-gray-400/30 dark:ring-gray-700/25 hover:ring-gray-400/60 dark:hover:ring-white/20 group-focus/link:border-2 group-focus/link:border-primary dark:group-focus/link:border-primary-light"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="size-3 shrink-0"><path d="M8.50001 6.827C8.14801 6.995 7.81801 7.225 7.52701 7.517L7.51701 7.527C6.13601 8.908 6.13601 11.146 7.51701 12.527L9.69201 14.702C11.073 16.083 13.311 16.083 14.692 14.702L14.702 14.692C16.083 13.311 16.083 11.073 14.702 9.692L13.771 8.761" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path><path d="M9.50002 11.173C9.85202 11.005 10.182 10.775 10.473 10.483L10.483 10.473C11.864 9.092 11.864 6.854 10.483 5.473L8.30802 3.298C6.92702 1.917 4.68902 1.917 3.30802 3.298L3.29802 3.308C1.91702 4.689 1.91702 6.927 3.29802 8.308L4.22902 9.239" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path></svg></div></a></div><span class="cursor-pointer">4. Plans and progress live in files in the repo</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>OpenAI:</strong> “It should always be possible to restart from only the ExecPlan.” (<a href="https://developers.openai.com/cookbook/articles/codex_exec_plans" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">Using PLANS.md for multi-hour problem solving</a>)</li>
<li><strong>Anthropic:</strong> “compaction isn’t sufficient.” Each session starts by reading a progress file and the git log. (<a href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/effective-harnesses-for-long-running-agents" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">Effective harnesses</a>)</li>
<li><strong>Lauren Tan:</strong> “Read the prior trail, don’t redo it.” (<a href="https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack/skills/poteto-mode" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">pstack playbooks</a>)</li>
</ul>
<span data-as="p">If the state only lives in the chat, the next session has to guess. In dev-skills, <code>deliver</code> keeps plan.md in ExecPlan format, committed with the code. When an upstream API error killed one of my long-running deliveries in Claude Code, I picked it up in MCode: a fresh session read plan.md and the git history and found where it had stopped in under half an hour.</span>
<h3 class="flex whitespace-pre-wrap group font-semibold" id="5-someone-else-decides-whether-it’s-right"><div class="absolute" tabindex="-1"><a href="#5-someone-else-decides-whether-it’s-right" class="-ml-10 flex items-center opacity-0 border-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100 focus:outline-0 group/link" aria-label="Navigate to header">​<div class="size-6 rounded-md flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-white/50 dark:bg-background-dark dark:brightness-[1.35] dark:ring-1 dark:hover:brightness-150 bg-white ring-1 ring-gray-400/30 dark:ring-gray-700/25 hover:ring-gray-400/60 dark:hover:ring-white/20 group-focus/link:border-2 group-focus/link:border-primary dark:group-focus/link:border-primary-light"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="size-3 shrink-0"><path d="M8.50001 6.827C8.14801 6.995 7.81801 7.225 7.52701 7.517L7.51701 7.527C6.13601 8.908 6.13601 11.146 7.51701 12.527L9.69201 14.702C11.073 16.083 13.311 16.083 14.692 14.702L14.702 14.692C16.083 13.311 16.083 11.073 14.702 9.692L13.771 8.761" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path><path d="M9.50002 11.173C9.85202 11.005 10.182 10.775 10.473 10.483L10.483 10.473C11.864 9.092 11.864 6.854 10.483 5.473L8.30802 3.298C6.92702 1.917 4.68902 1.917 3.30802 3.298L3.29802 3.308C1.91702 4.689 1.91702 6.927 3.29802 8.308L4.22902 9.239" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path></svg></div></a></div><span class="cursor-pointer">5. Someone else decides whether it’s right</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Anthropic:</strong> “Out of the box, Claude is a poor QA agent.” Their fix: “Separating the agent doing the work from the agent judging it proves to be a strong lever.” (<a href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/harness-design-long-running-apps" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">Harness design for long-running application development</a>)</li>
<li><strong>OpenAI:</strong> “we’ve pushed almost all review effort towards being handled agent-to-agent.” (<a href="https://openai.com/index/harness-engineering/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">Harness engineering</a>)</li>
<li><strong>Lauren Tan:</strong> “Run a unit’s verifier on a different model family from its worker.” (<a href="https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack/skills" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">pstack skills</a>)</li>
</ul>
<span data-as="p">The author’s blind spots live in its context, and models from the same family tend to share them. dev-skills has three layers: a fresh subagent after each milestone, another model family for the gap check and the final verification, and me, reading the decision list before I merge. On my first real run, the first cross-family verification caught an issue that two rounds of same-model checks had missed.</span>
<h3 class="flex whitespace-pre-wrap group font-semibold" id="6-when-the-agent-gets-stuck-fix-the-repo-not-the-prompt"><div class="absolute" tabindex="-1"><a href="#6-when-the-agent-gets-stuck-fix-the-repo-not-the-prompt" class="-ml-10 flex items-center opacity-0 border-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100 focus:outline-0 group/link" aria-label="Navigate to header">​<div class="size-6 rounded-md flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-white/50 dark:bg-background-dark dark:brightness-[1.35] dark:ring-1 dark:hover:brightness-150 bg-white ring-1 ring-gray-400/30 dark:ring-gray-700/25 hover:ring-gray-400/60 dark:hover:ring-white/20 group-focus/link:border-2 group-focus/link:border-primary dark:group-focus/link:border-primary-light"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="size-3 shrink-0"><path d="M8.50001 6.827C8.14801 6.995 7.81801 7.225 7.52701 7.517L7.51701 7.527C6.13601 8.908 6.13601 11.146 7.51701 12.527L9.69201 14.702C11.073 16.083 13.311 16.083 14.692 14.702L14.702 14.692C16.083 13.311 16.083 11.073 14.702 9.692L13.771 8.761" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path><path d="M9.50002 11.173C9.85202 11.005 10.182 10.775 10.473 10.483L10.483 10.473C11.864 9.092 11.864 6.854 10.483 5.473L8.30802 3.298C6.92702 1.917 4.68902 1.917 3.30802 3.298L3.29802 3.308C1.91702 4.689 1.91702 6.927 3.29802 8.308L4.22902 9.239" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path></svg></div></a></div><span class="cursor-pointer">6. When the agent gets stuck, fix the repo, not the prompt</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>OpenAI:</strong> “When the agent struggles, we treat it as a signal: identify what is missing—tools, guardrails, documentation—and feed it back into the repository.” (<a href="https://openai.com/index/harness-engineering/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">Harness engineering</a>)</li>
<li><strong>Anthropic:</strong> CLAUDE.md instructions “are advisory,” while hooks “are deterministic and guarantee the action happens.” (<a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/best-practices" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">Claude Code best practices</a>)</li>
<li><strong>Lauren Tan:</strong> “The instruction is the symptom.” (<a href="https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack/skills/principle-encode-lessons-in-structure" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">Encode Lessons in Structure</a>)</li>
</ul>
<span data-as="p">A rule in a prompt is a request the next agent may skip; a rule in code runs every time. In dev-skills, two scripts enforce what must always hold: <code>freeze.mjs</code> pins spec.md and verify.md, and <code>check-delivery.mjs</code> gates the result. Phase D turns each run’s friction into repo tooling.</span>
<h3 class="flex whitespace-pre-wrap group font-semibold" id="7-add-complexity-only-when-it-pays-one-piece-at-a-time"><div class="absolute" tabindex="-1"><a href="#7-add-complexity-only-when-it-pays-one-piece-at-a-time" class="-ml-10 flex items-center opacity-0 border-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100 focus:outline-0 group/link" aria-label="Navigate to header">​<div class="size-6 rounded-md flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-white/50 dark:bg-background-dark dark:brightness-[1.35] dark:ring-1 dark:hover:brightness-150 bg-white ring-1 ring-gray-400/30 dark:ring-gray-700/25 hover:ring-gray-400/60 dark:hover:ring-white/20 group-focus/link:border-2 group-focus/link:border-primary dark:group-focus/link:border-primary-light"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="size-3 shrink-0"><path d="M8.50001 6.827C8.14801 6.995 7.81801 7.225 7.52701 7.517L7.51701 7.527C6.13601 8.908 6.13601 11.146 7.51701 12.527L9.69201 14.702C11.073 16.083 13.311 16.083 14.692 14.702L14.702 14.692C16.083 13.311 16.083 11.073 14.702 9.692L13.771 8.761" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path><path d="M9.50002 11.173C9.85202 11.005 10.182 10.775 10.473 10.483L10.483 10.473C11.864 9.092 11.864 6.854 10.483 5.473L8.30802 3.298C6.92702 1.917 4.68902 1.917 3.30802 3.298L3.29802 3.308C1.91702 4.689 1.91702 6.927 3.29802 8.308L4.22902 9.239" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path></svg></div></a></div><span class="cursor-pointer">7. Add complexity only when it pays, one piece at a time</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Anthropic:</strong> they recommend “finding the simplest solution possible, and only increasing complexity when needed.” (<a href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/building-effective-agents" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">Building effective agents</a>)</li>
<li><strong>OpenAI:</strong> “Prefer a narrow correction to accumulating universal rules for every observed example.” (<a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/skills/src/assets/samples/skill-creator/SKILL.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">Codex skill-creator</a>)</li>
<li><strong>Lauren Tan:</strong> pstack PR #419 cut 19 instructions. “Each cut held up in A/B runs on tasks that exercise it, with and without the text.” (<a href="https://github.com/cursor/plugins/pull/419" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">PR #419</a>)</li>
</ul>
<span data-as="p">I learned this one the hard way. After each trial run I added a rule and a script to check it. <code>deliver</code> went from 3 scripts to 11, and its instructions grew by about 70%. Then I cut back to 1 script and less than half the instructions. The whole arc took 32 versions of the workflow in four days.</span>
<h2 class="flex whitespace-pre-wrap group font-semibold" id="how-to-use-it"><div class="absolute" tabindex="-1"><a href="#how-to-use-it" class="-ml-10 flex items-center opacity-0 border-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100 focus:outline-0 group/link" aria-label="Navigate to header">​<div class="size-6 rounded-md flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-white/50 dark:bg-background-dark dark:brightness-[1.35] dark:ring-1 dark:hover:brightness-150 bg-white ring-1 ring-gray-400/30 dark:ring-gray-700/25 hover:ring-gray-400/60 dark:hover:ring-white/20 group-focus/link:border-2 group-focus/link:border-primary dark:group-focus/link:border-primary-light"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="size-3 shrink-0"><path d="M8.50001 6.827C8.14801 6.995 7.81801 7.225 7.52701 7.517L7.51701 7.527C6.13601 8.908 6.13601 11.146 7.51701 12.527L9.69201 14.702C11.073 16.083 13.311 16.083 14.692 14.702L14.702 14.692C16.083 13.311 16.083 11.073 14.702 9.692L13.771 8.761" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path><path d="M9.50002 11.173C9.85202 11.005 10.182 10.775 10.473 10.483L10.483 10.473C11.864 9.092 11.864 6.854 10.483 5.473L8.30802 3.298C6.92702 1.917 4.68902 1.917 3.30802 3.298L3.29802 3.308C1.91702 4.689 1.91702 6.927 3.29802 8.308L4.22902 9.239" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path></svg></div></a></div><span class="cursor-pointer">How to use it</span></h2>
<span data-as="p"><strong>What you need</strong></span>
<ul>
<li>Models from two families. I develop in MCode and hand the checks to Codex, a different model family from the one I run in MCode; Claude Code plus Codex works too. The gap check and the final verification must come from the family that didn’t do the work, through a CLI that’s installed and logged in.</li>
<li>Node.js 24, git, and <code>gh</code> or <code>glab</code>.</li>
<li>An app the agent can start, operate and observe from a worktree (phase A). The <a href="https://github.com/coder-xieshijie/dev-skills/blob/main/docs/repository-readiness.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">repository readiness guide</a> in dev-skills covers what that takes, and Lauren’s <a href="https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack/skills/create-verification-skill" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link">create-verification-skill</a> is a good place to start.</li>
</ul>
<span data-as="p"><strong>Install</strong> by asking your agent. Paste this into MCode, Claude Code or Codex:</span>
<div class="code-block mt-5 mb-8 not-prose rounded-2xl relative group min-w-0 print:print-color-exact text-gray-950 dark:text-gray-50 codeblock-light border border-gray-950/10 dark:border-white/10 dark:twoslash-dark bg-transparent dark:bg-transparent" data-has-floating-buttons="" numberOfLines="5" language="text"><div data-floating-buttons="true" class="absolute top-3 right-4 flex items-center gap-1.5 print:hidden"><div class="z-10 select-none" id="base-ui-_R_1tbapbb9qnpfb39p7b9snpfiutb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><button class="size-6.5 flex items-center justify-center rounded-md group/code-snippet-feedback-button [.code-block:not(:has([data-fade-overlay]))_[data-floating-buttons]_&amp;]:bg-gray-100 dark:[.code-block:not(:has([data-fade-overlay]))_[data-floating-buttons]_&amp;]:bg-gray-800" id="code-snippet-feedback-button" aria-label="Report incorrect code"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="size-4 shrink-0 text-gray-400 group-hover/code-snippet-feedback-button:text-gray-500 dark:text-white/40 dark:group-hover/code-snippet-feedback-button:text-white/60"><path d="M9 5.431V9.569" stroke="currentColor" width="1.5" linecap="round" linejoin="round"></path><path d="M9 11.417C8.449 11.417 8 11.866 8 12.417C8 12.968 8.449 13.417 9 13.417C9.551 13.417 10 12.968 10 12.417C10 11.866 9.551 11.417 9 11.417Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"></path><path d="M10.968 2.25H7.03301C6.50301 2.25 5.99401 2.461 5.61901 2.836L2.83701 5.618C2.46201 5.993 2.25101 6.502 2.25101 7.032V10.967C2.25101 11.497 2.46201 12.006 2.83701 12.381L5.61901 15.163C5.99401 15.538 6.50301 15.749 7.03301 15.749H10.968C11.498 15.749 12.007 15.538 12.382 15.163L15.164 12.381C15.539 12.006 15.75 11.497 15.75 10.967V7.032C15.75 6.502 15.539 5.993 15.164 5.618L12.382 2.836C12.007 2.461 11.498 2.25 10.968 2.25Z" stroke="currentColor" 